adjudication.rationale:
In the newly added API route `apps/web/pages/api/webhook/app-credential.ts`, the decrypted payload is immediately passed to `JSON.parse(...)`:

```ts
const keys = JSON.parse(
  symmetricDecrypt(reqBody.keys, process.env.CALCOM_APP_CREDENTIAL_ENCRYPTION_KEY || "")
);
```

There is no try/catch around either `symmetricDecrypt(...)` or `JSON.parse(...)`. If decryption yields a non-JSON string (e.g., wrong/missing key, empty/garbled plaintext), `JSON.parse` will throw a `SyntaxError`, which will bubble up and result in an uncaught 500 response from the Next.js API handler. This is a real correctness/robustness defect exposed by the diff.
